# The exports of a display driver, at the ordinals GDI and USER look them
# up by, and the description GDI reads (the technology and the aspect
# ratio: "DISPLAY : <ratio>, <x dpi>, <y dpi>"). The module must be named
# DISPLAY, which the output name DISPLAY.DRV gives.
option description 'DISPLAY : 100, 96, 96'
# The mouse interrupt moves the cursor (MoveCursor), so the code and data
# are loaded at start and never move.
segment type code preload fixed
segment type data preload fixed
